content.text:
```js
for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
  i;
}
```

Read the three parts as:

- start `i` at `0`
- continue while `i < 3`
- increase `i` by `1` after each round

content.question:
How many times does the loop body run?

```js
for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
  i;
}
```

feedback.correct:
Verified! Reference solution:
```js
for (let i = 1; i <= 3; i++) {
  i;
}
```

content.text:
What is wrong here?

```js
let i = 0;
while (i < 3) {
  i;
}
```

The condition starts true, but the value never changes, so the condition never becomes false. That is an infinite loop.
